Sedef Amp @VERSION@ for macOS
=============================

Open-source guitar amp and effects suite, with Sedef MIDI, which plays MIDI instruments from
your guitar. macOS 11 or later, Apple silicon and Intel.


INSTALL

1. Double-click "Install Sedef Amp".
2. Pick what you want (all is selected) and enter your password when asked. Untick
   "Sedef MIDI" to leave it out.
3. Rescan plugins in your DAW. Sedef shows up as "Sedef Amp" and "Sedef MIDI" by "Sedef".

Where things go:
  Standalone app   /Applications/Sedef Amp.app
  VST3             /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/VST3/Sedef Amp.vst3
  Audio Unit       /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/Components/Sedef Amp.component
  CLAP             /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/CLAP/Sedef Amp.clap
  Sedef MIDI       /Applications/Sedef MIDI.app
                   /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/VST3/Sedef MIDI.vst3
                   /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/Components/Sedef MIDI.component
                   /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/Components/Sedef MIDI Instrument.component
                   /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/CLAP/Sedef MIDI.clap


SEDEF MIDI

Sedef MIDI turns your guitar's DI into MIDI notes in real time, one note at a time: play a bass
line on the guitar and hear it on any MIDI instrument. Open Sedef MIDI.app and pick your
interface's input, or put the Sedef MIDI plugin on your guitar track. In Logic Pro, load
"Sedef MIDI (Instrument)" on an instrument track with the guitar track as its side chain.
Setup guide: https://github.com/mr-kaynak/sedef-amp/blob/main/docs/midi.md


"INSTALL SEDEF AMP" NOT OPENED?

@MACOS_FIRST_LAUNCH@


UPDATING

From this version on, Sedef updates itself: when a new version is out, click Update now in
Sedef's Updates panel and enter your password. It installs over the formats you have, and
Sedef MIDI if you have it; you don't need to delete anything first.

This installer also replaces an older installed version. If you copied Sedef Amp into
~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins by hand (version 0.1.0 shipped that way), run "Uninstall Sedef Amp"
first so your DAW doesn't list two copies. Your presets are kept.


UNINSTALL

Double-click "Uninstall Sedef Amp" (it opens in Terminal and asks before removing anything).
It removes Sedef Amp and Sedef MIDI. If macOS blocks it, open Terminal and run:
  bash "/Volumes/Sedef Amp @VERSION@/Uninstall Sedef Amp.command"
To remove Sedef MIDI only, add --midi:
  bash "/Volumes/Sedef Amp @VERSION@/Uninstall Sedef Amp.command" --midi

Presets and settings live in ~/Library/Application Support/Sedef and are not removed.


